# behavior: a dependency's declarations keep one identity through every module that republishes them: a type published at its declaring module, at a directory facade and at the package root is one type to its consumer, a value spelled through one path is accepted where another is expected, a model reached only as the element type of another model's list field has its declaration's fields and methods even when the root publishes a different model under its name, and a pattern names a type imported after the signature that returns it (#1561); a module that re-exports a dependency's renamed function under a further name hands its consumers a callable name (#1751); a dependency whose root-level and nested modules re-export another module's declarations spelled from the package root (`crate.inner`), through two modules and under a new name, for a function, a model, an enum and a const, builds, and its consumer uses each name through every module that publishes it (#1561); and a library can call a sibling module through a bare module import while its own script shares that module (#2237)
